  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 8.1. Increased capacity of member States to develop new or reformed sustainable national social protection strategies, policies or legal frameworks to extend coverage and enhance benefit adequacy</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In June 2021, the Cabinet adopted a new Lesotho National Social Security Policy (LNSSP) 2021 and its action plan, developed in consultation with the social partners. The policy is guided by international labour standards. The Policy aims at establishing a comprehensive and inclusive national social security system based on social insurance principles. It seeks to extend coverage to all (the current system covers only civil servants) and introduce new and/or enhanced benefits -  pensions, maternity, employment injury, unemployment and sickness. The LNSSP proposes the establishment of the national social security organisation to enhance coordination and service delivery. The ILO provided technical support to the national tripartite social security task team to ensure that the development of the national social security policy and action plan was guided by international labour standards. This includes background technical papers (including an actuarial valuation), review of the draft policy and social security bill, support to tripartite capacity building and consultations (July 2019).</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">8.1.1. Number of member States with new or revised national social protection policies to extend coverage, enhance comprehensiveness and/or increase adequacy of benefits</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
